# This file is intentionally assignment-free. Do not copy it to `.dev.vars`.
#
# Local API credentials belong in the macOS Keychain service managed by:
#
#   pnpm --filter @zenguy/api secrets:list
#   pnpm --filter @zenguy/api secrets:set -- NAME
#   pnpm --filter @zenguy/api secrets:verify
#
# `pnpm --filter @zenguy/api dev` serves those values from memory through a
# private FIFO; the seed uses an anonymous file descriptor. Neither path writes
# a regular plaintext dotenv file or falls back to `.dev.vars`. Non-secret
# defaults remain in `wrangler.jsonc`.
#
# Keep `ENCRYPTION_PREVIOUS_KEYS` only while retained ciphertext or an approved
# backup still depends on an old key. The Paddle core group is all-or-none, and
# its optional alert-credit product/price IDs are a pair. See README.md for the
# complete inventory and migration procedure.
#
# Remote-only Access binding inventory (never needed for local runs):
# - CF_ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN: exact https://<team>.cloudflareaccess.com origin
# - CF_ACCESS_AUD: audience tag of the Access application protecting staging
# - CF_RUNNER_ACCESS_AUD: production service-only runner application audience
